<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "A P2P session always runs in a browser tab of its own — the chat has no window for one. The card in the private message is the door; following it gives the session the whole window and leaves the conversation where it was."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_btn_link}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "Sharing the address")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "Share mints a link you can paste anywhere. The link names the session and never grants access to it: only the two people already in it can enter, and anyone else who follows it gets a card explaining that."
  )}
</p>

<.help_h4 icon={:icon_window_restore}>{dgettext("help_p2p", "One window at a time")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_p2p",
    "A session can only be live in one of your windows. Opening it somewhere else moves it there, and the window that lost it says so and offers Bring it back here — which is why the conversation offers a way to the tab you already have instead of a second one. Closing the tab is not the same as ending the session: you have about half a minute to come back to the address before it closes itself. Only End session, which asks first, is final straight away."
  )}
</p>

<p>
  {dgettext("help_p2p", "See also:")}
  <.help_link topic="feature-p2p-in-chat">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "P2P Sessions in Chat")}
  </.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-p2p-starting-room">
    {dgettext("help_p2p", "P2P Starting Room")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
